15, patients who had asthma documented in the medical record accounted for 9.5%26#37; of all ED visits in the United States, with the highest percentage for children aged 5–17 years (13.6%26#37;), compared with 6.6%26#37; for children aged 0–4 years, 9.9%26#37; for adults aged 18–64 years, and 6.5%26#37; for those aged ≥65 years. Among those aged 0–4 years, boys were more likely than girls to have a visit with asthma recorded, but for the older age groups, 18–64 and ≥65, women with asthma documented were more likely than men to have an ED visit. The difference by sex for those aged 5–17 years was not statistically significant.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":614,"renderedHeight":395,"naturalWidth":614,"naturalHeight":395,"loading":null,"decoding":"async","altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 693 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":30688},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/5.0/img/logo/cdc-logo-tag-right.svg","alt":"Centers for Disease Control and Prevention","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":283,"renderedHeight":66,"naturalWidth":827,"naturalHeight":193,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":4780},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/contrib/libs/cdc/c2r/crlogo.svg","alt":"Content Credentials logo","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":25,"renderedHeight":150,"naturalWidth":150,"naturalHeight":150,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":1490}]}}